  {
   "n": 4,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>The image channel selectivity of superheterodyne receiver depends upon,</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "IF amplifier only."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "RF and IF amplifiers only."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Preselector, RF and IF amplifiers."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Preselector and RF amplifiers only."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(d)<br />\nThe image rejection should be achieved before IF stage because ones the image frequency enters<br />\ninto IF amplifier, it becomes impossible to remove it from wanted signal. So, image channel<br />\nselectivity depends upon preselector and RF amplifiers only and is achieved by tuning the filter<br />\nto attenuate the image frequency. The IF amplifier helps in rejection of adjacent channel frequency<br />\nand not image frequency.</p>"
  },
